        <mxCell id="resolvesBox" value="&lt;b style=&quot;color:#D64309&quot;&gt;What temporal precedence + immutability resolves:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Only HRT is a modifiable &lt;b&gt;late&lt;/b&gt; event. The other edges point outward from genetic/developmental nodes — they can&#39;t absorb credit that belongs to HRT." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF4E6;fontColor=#3F4444;strokeColor=#D64309;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=13;fontFamily=Arial;arcSize=8;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="960" y="620" width="680" height="90" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="legendBox" value="&lt;b&gt;WHAT THE OBJECT MODEL CARRIES THAT THE FLAT TABLE DOES NOT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Immutability at birth&lt;/b&gt; — family history can only be a &lt;i&gt;source&lt;/i&gt;, never a sink.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Developmental timestamps&lt;/b&gt; — menarche &amp; first birth anchor to specific ages, not flags.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Policy-lever events&lt;/b&gt; — HRT start dates separable from diagnosis, so the modifiable edge is identifiable." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F6F8FC;fontColor=#3F4444;strokeColor=#CDCDCD;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Arial;arcSize=8;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="770" width="1600" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
